{"id": "f3eee97b-456f-4232-8eb8-2a1a8dc84dc2", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Finding stale long-lived credentials with Bedrock access across IAM is token-heavy work, so I should delegate this scan to a sub-agent rather than doing it directly. I'll share my plan first, then figure out which accounts to include—starting with the agent space account, though associations might span others.

Since sub-agents are read-only and I can't modify permissions or delete anything anyway, this is purely a listing task, so I just need to craft a clear prompt for the sub-agent to run.

"}]}

{"id": "e96dd663-99b2-40a7-b42b-3c5b9caa4f1f", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check IAM for long-lived credentials with Bedrock access: access keys, plus Bedrock API keys, which are service-specific credentials. For each one I'll look at when it was last used. This means scanning users, their policies, and credential usage data, so I'm running it in the background and will summarize the results for you.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_Um2aLN9ntztgEQOQBzep4Q", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-stale-credentials", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Identify long-lived credentials that grant Amazon Bedrock access and have NOT been used in the last 90 days, and assess which are safe to remove. READ-ONLY: do not modify or delete anything.",
  "context": "User wants a cleanup list. Long-lived credentials = IAM user access keys (AKIA...) and IAM service-specific credentials, including Amazon Bedrock API keys (long-term, ServiceName bedrock.amazonaws.com, created via iam create-service-specific-credential). Short-term Bedrock API keys and role sessions are not in scope. Current time is 2026-11-25T08:22:00Z, so the cutoff is 2026-08-27T08:22:00Z. Use list_associations to find the AWS accounts available to this agent space (primary account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1) and cover all monitor/source accounts you can access. IAM is global; use us-east-1.",
  "resources": ["IAM users, access keys, service-specific credentials in all accessible accounts", "Agent space account 012345678901_1"],
  "timeframe": "Last 90 days (cutoff 2026-08-27T08:22:00Z)",
  "criteria": "1) Enumerate IAM users and determine which have Bedrock access: via attached managed policies (e.g. AmazonBedrockFullAccess, AmazonBedrockLimitedAccess, AmazonBedrockReadOnly, AmazonBedrockMantleFullAccess etc.), inline policies, and group-inherited policies that allow bedrock:* / bedrock-runtime / bedrock-mantle actions, or wildcard (*) actions/AdministratorAccess (flag these separately as 'implicit/broad access'). Also check permissions boundaries that could restrict. 2) Also list all service-specific credentials for bedrock.amazonaws.com (list_service_specific_credentials) with status, creation date, and expiration; use last-used info if available. 3) For each access key, use get_access_key_last_used (LastUsedDate, ServiceName, Region) and key status/created date; for credentials never used, note creation date. 4) Report those with Bedrock access whose last use is older than 90 days or never used (and created >90 days ago). 5) For each, give a safe-to-remove assessment: SAFE (inactive/never used and older than 90 days, no recent use at all), CAUTION (last used 90+ days ago but could be periodic/seasonal e.g. quarterly jobs, or key is the user's only credential, or user is a service/automation account by naming/tags), or DO NOT REMOVE/UNKNOWN (cannot verify). Note caveat: last-used data only reflects activity since tracking began (April 2015, region-specific) and service-specific credential last-use may not be tracked; optionally cross-check the IAM credential report. Also mention whether the key is Active or Inactive, and the owning user, tags, and whether the user has console access. Return a concise table per account: user, credential type/ID (key ID is fine, never secrets), status, created, last used (date/service/region), how Bedrock access is granted, recommendation + reason. Include summary counts and any accounts or calls that failed due to permissions."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Scan IAM for stale Bedrock-capable credentials"}], "created_at": null}

